  "body": "First time on the market in over 35 years\r\n\r\nKey Highlights\r\n\r\n• 759m² Freehold Land – Zoned Residential - Mixed Housing Suburban with options to renovate, add value, landbank, or explore future development potential.\r\n\r\n• Elevated Sea Views – Wide sea views enjoyed from the master bedroom, kitchen, dining room, lounge, and warm conservatory leading out to the large north-facing deck.\r\n\r\n• Top School Zones – In zone for Rangitoto College, Murrays Bay Intermediate, and Mairangi Bay School (all within easy walking distance).\r\n\r\n• Prime Location & Lifestyle – Perfect for morning walks to Mairangi Bay Beach and surrounding local parks/coastal tracks, with close proximity to supermarkets, gyms, dining options, local retailers, Park & Ride, and motorway links.\r\n\r\n• Flexible 4-Bedroom Layout – 3 upstairs bedrooms plus an upgraded downstairs room (originally shown as a teenage room in council plans, upgraded with an elevated floor and built-in wardrobe, suitable as a 4th bedroom, second living area, home office, or studio).\r\n\r\n• Established Garden & Orchard – Features a variety of established fruit trees (persimmon, orange, lemon, feijoa, plum, grape, and cherry) plus a 3x5m vegetable garden, additional planting areas, pathways, flower beds, and compost area.\r\n\r\nOwned by the same family for more than three decades, this classic 1969-built home offers a rare opportunity to secure a freehold property in the highly sought-after Rangitoto College Zone.\r\n\r\nThe home features a flexible layout with sea views enjoyed from the main living areas, extending through a warm, sunny conservatory to the large north-facing deck with natural greenery providing privacy. Enjoy lovely morning walks down to Mairangi Bay Beach and nearby parks, taking full advantage of the enviable coastal lifestyle. Downstairs offers excellent versatility for extended family, a work-from-home setup, or extra living space.\r\n\r\nWith excellent street exposure, generous off-street parking, and the possibility of a tandem garage, the property may also appeal to those considering a home business, subject to council guidance. With the right renovations, there is an opportunity to unlock the property's full potential and add value over time.\r\n\r\nThis home offers a rare combination of location, land size, school zones, coastal lifestyle, convenience, and future potential.\r\n\r\nCV $1,575,000= $1,375,000 ( Land Value )+ $200,000 ( Improvement Value )\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
